<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Sustaining capital expenditures</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Sustaining capital expenditures are defined as
those expenditures which do not increase payable mineral production at a mine site and excludes all expenditures at the Company&rsquo;s
projects and certain expenditures at the Company&rsquo;s operating sites which are deemed expansionary in nature. Expansionary capital
expenditures are expenditures that are deemed expansionary in nature. The following table reconciles sustaining capital expenditures and
expansionary capital expenditures to the Company&rsquo;s additions to mineral, properties, plant and equipment (or total capital expenditures):</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

